# mbsync's configuration, and the machine ships it EMPTY OF ACCOUNTS. A row
# here would be a mailbox somebody else chose.
#
# EMPTY LINES DELIMIT SECTIONS — that is mbsync's own rule, not a style. When
# you uncomment a block below, keep its lines adjacent and keep the blank line
# between blocks, or the Channel lands in the Store above it and mbsync
# reports a key it does not understand.
#
# THE MAILDIR ROOT IS ~/Mail AND THREE PROGRAMS AGREE ON IT: mbsync writes
# there, ~/.config/notmuch/default/config indexes there, and an aerc account
# reads there. Move it here and you move it in all three, or the index is of a
# directory nothing fills.
#
# THIS FILE IS MODE 600 because PassCmd's output is a password and a Pass line
# is one outright. `notmuch new` runs `mbsync -a` from its pre-new hook, so
# once a Channel below is live, fetching is something you never type.
#
# NO XOAUTH2. isync reaches it only through cyrus-sasl, which this image does
# not carry, so an account whose provider has withdrawn application passwords
# cannot be synchronised by this binary at all.

# Defaults for every Channel that does not say otherwise. Expunge None keeps a
# deletion local until you ask for it; Create Both lets either side make a
# folder the other has.
#Expunge None
#Create Both

#MaildirStore local
#Path ~/Mail/
#Inbox ~/Mail/INBOX
#SubFolders Verbatim

#IMAPStore mail
#Host imap.example.org
#User you@example.org
#PassCmd "pass show mail/example.org"
#TLSType IMAPS
#CertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt

#Channel mail
#Far :mail:
#Near :local:
#Patterns *
#SyncState *

# `mbsync -a` runs every Channel in every Group. The pre-new hook calls exactly
# that, so a Channel added here needs nothing else to be fetched.
#Group all
#Channels mail
